WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:04.340
A door can do only one
thing: turn about its hinges.

2
00:00:04.390 --> 00:00:07.200
Push on its edge, straight
towards the hinges,

3
00:00:07.250 --> 00:00:10.990
and however hard you push,
it will not turn at all.

4
00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:14.790
So a force can be large,
and still turn nothing.

5
00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:17.210
Size alone is not enough.

6
00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:18.610
Look at any door.

7
00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:21.620
The handle is on the
edge far from the hinges.

8
00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:23.370
Why not right next to them?

9
00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:28.990
In this mission, you'll meet torque: the
turning effect of a force about an axis.

10
00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:33.530
Then you'll find the lever arm, and see
why the angle of a push matters as much

11
00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:34.950
as its size.

12
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:39.810
Your mission: explain why the handle
goes on the edge far from the hinges.
